Furthermore, as outlined in 15 U.S.C. 1681n, the credit reporting agency faces civil liability for willful noncompliance, with damages incurred by the consumer due to such failure resulting in compensation of {$1000.00} or the actual damages sustained, whichever is greater. Acceptance of payment in the form of a check is stipulated, with a request for compensation to be provided within 24 hours of receiving this dispute letter.

Moreover, under 15 U.S.C. 1681g, the consumer possesses the unequivocal right to demand disclosure of all documents recorded and retained by the credit reporting agency pertaining to the accounts reported on the credit report.

