15 U.S. Code 1681a ( d ) ( 2 ) : Exclusions The term "" consumer report '' does not include certain types of information, such as transactions or experiences between the consumer and the person making the report. 
15 U.S. Code 1681s2 : Responsibilities of Furnishers of Information to Consumer Reporting Agencies 15 U.S. Code 1681i : Procedure in Case of Disputed Accuracy 15 U.S.C. 1681i ( a ) ( 5 ) ( A ) : Requirement for Deletion or Correction If an item is found to be inaccurate or can not be verified, it must be deleted or corrected by the credit reporting agency. In this case, I request deletion of the account.

15 U.S.C. 1681s-2 ( b ) ( 1 ) : Responsibilities of Furnishers Furnishers must conduct an investigation when they receive a notice of dispute from a credit reporting agency. If the information is found to be inaccurate, they must notify all credit reporting agencies to which they provided the information. 
Additionally, if XXXX has reported a balance for a debt that was charged off and potentially canceled ( as evidenced by a Form 1099-C ), this constitutes inaccurate reporting.

Request for Permanent Removal Due to the multiple violations and the significant harm these inaccuracies have caused to my creditworthiness, I request the following resolutions : Immediate and permanent removal of the inaccurate account from my credit report. 
Notification once the inaccurate account is removed. 
Rectification of any negative impact on my credit score and restoration to reflect my true creditworthiness. 
