9261769,2024-06-14,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Information belongs to someone else,"I, XXXX XXXX XXXX, affirm my status as a living individual. I am reaching out to address a matter of significant concern regarding my credit report. Upon reviewing the information contained within, I have discovered several discrepancies that I believe require immediate attention. It has come to my attention that certain accounts listed on my credit report do not belong to me, and their inclusion is not only inaccurate but also violates my rights as a consumer. Allow me to elaborate on the specific issues I have identified and the laws that support my claim : **15 U.S Code 1681a ( 4 ) - Consumer Right to Privacy : ** The presence of fraudulent accounts on my credit report constitutes an intrusion into my privacy rights. I firmly believe that I have the sole authority to determine what information is private and should be shared on my credit report.

