This is considered an unauthorized use since I received zero benefit. Pursuant to 18 U.S.C. 8, every coupon, bill, and certificate of indebtedness, both public and private used for personal, family, and household use are obligations of the United States. This complaint also serves as a Notice of Breach of Fiduciary Duty ( U.C.C. 3-307 ). I continue to submit complaints to the CFPB but if it doesnt resolve my case then a SEC complaint will be filed pursuant to 17 CFR 240.15c1-2 and 17 CFR 240.10b-5. Additionally, an IRS complaint for abusive tax schemes involving the SEC-filed trust arrangement for breach of securities and securities fraud will be filed.

The use of Federal Reserve Notes is unlawful and can not fulfill this purpose. Furthermore, I have noticed that XXXX XXXX XXXX  has been redeeming the dividends as non-cash items ( 12 CFR 210.2 ( k ) / 12 CFR 229.2 ( u ) ( 4 ) ).

Pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1691 ( C ), assuming civil liability pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1691 ( K ). 
