9315745,2024-06-21,Student loan,Federal student loan servicing,Dealing with your lender or servicer,Problem with customer service,"I made a large lump sum payment of {$37000.00} to my student loans that was posted to my checking account on XX/XX/year>. Once that payment was processed on my Mohela account ( it was no longer pending ), I requested a proof of payment document or financial transaction summary. I needed that proof of payment by XX/XX/year> and was sure that I had given myself plenty of time ( as I had done this process multiple times in the past ). Mohela completed my request and sent me an email on XX/XX/year>, stating that I could now log in to my online Mohela account and download that document. However, when I went to log in the weekend of XX/XX/XXXX, I received a "" system-platform transfer notice '' stating that my Mohela loans were being transferred to the new platform and I could no longer access my Mohela account. I eventually confirmed with Mohela customer service representatives that my account began the transfer to the new Mohela/Dept of Education platform on XX/XX/year>. Therefore, I would have never been able to electronically access this proof of payment XXXX. 

I contacted Mohela on Monday, XX/XX/XXXX to try to have the document sent to me another way. I was told they could only mail the document and there was no other way to help me. I initially took them at their word and attempted to resolve the issue on my end. I am a XXXX XXXX  for the XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, and I am enrolled in the Education Debt Reduction Program ( EDRP ). Payments I make towards my loans, up to $ XXXX, are refunded to me at the end of each year, as long as I provide proof of payment. I gathered my bank statements and took screenshots of my loan balances on the Department of Education website to show the decreased loan balances, but worried this would still not be accepted as adequate proof of payment by the EDRP.

Since Wednesday, XX/XX/XXXX is XXXX, I had to wait until Thursday to attempt to contact Mohela again. I took most of the day off work in order to call Mohela and wait on hold, and because I was so nauseated and distressed ( at this point I essentially thought I was about to lose over {$37000.00} ). I was again told that they could not send me the proof of payment in a way that would arrive by XX/XX/XXXX. They told me the document was created and they could mail it ( which I had already requested they do on Monday, XX/XX/XXXX when I first called ), but there was no way to send this to me electronically. 

