9361304,2024-06-27,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account status incorrect,"I'm actually writing this as a complaint regarding the hypocritical expectations of credit reporting agencies, specifically regarding opening new lines of credit. The credit industry increases your score only when you have good standing accounts and a low credit usage ratio. So raising your credit limit ( otherwise proving that you have said good standing with the company ) should only increase your score. The excuse that a "" hard inquiry '' should temporarily lower your score, even though it's proving that you qualify for higher credit, is not only hypocritical, it's unethical in a country that is already struggling with personal debt. In addition, the suggestion that opening a new account should actually lower your "" average '' credit history is ridiculous and only serves to further harm people 's financial stability. The first account opened is still the first account. Opening a new one doesn't change that fact. Making the length of credit history an average of when the accounts were opened is completely illogical. Credit reporting agencies should be held accountable for imposing hypocritical rules that make it so that if you do what they want and maintain good standing credit, as shown by the banks ' decision to grant you a new line of credit or increase your current limit, you are penalized for it. This is unfair, illogical, and, as stated, overall unethical. I'm sure this complaint will not make any difference, and I'm sure that the rulemakers care nothing for their impact on the rest of the country, basically everyone who isn't them. But it needs to be said regardless.",,"EQUIFAX, INC.",MD,21221,,Web,2024-06-27,Closed with explanation,Yes
